/caveman

Use /visualize a lot to show information in a nice way to me.

Open to your suggestions. If have a good idea, stop and tell me. Even if I give direct command, you stop and say why maybe not good idea. I don't understand typscript/web-app/api architectures very well; explain in simple language.

Use jj. Make commits with short one-line messages. Squash and group commits when see fit, and make parallel commits if you like. If change incremental, squashing instead of new commit. Use jj's nice feature set, and prefer merging to rebasing. When completely done with task, move to empty commit. Move bookmarks like wip/... (never main, don't push) to the top. Clean up workspaces AND bookmark if appropriate. NOTE: take care with parallel commands and creating divergent commits; fix those immediately. And creating child commits on top of commits with no description is not allowed.

AGENTS.md and other content is intentionally not tracked (see .git/info/exclude).

Use uv for Python.

Prefer opening the built-in browser.

Tests are good! Endless smoke tests, "regression tests" for feature deletions, etc, much less good. Tests should be focused, not slop.

Backwards compatibility never main concern, prefer simplicity and overall best design-choice. Keep codebase simple. Less is more. Again: always evaluate if less code can do the job.

{{- if eq .profile "nas" }}

## CerpacNAS limits

- Work only below `/root/Projects` and the task's `jw` workspace.
- Root login is intentional, but never use `sudo`, Docker, system package changes, or dangerous sandbox/approval bypass flags. `--skip-git-repo-check` is allowed only for a secondary JJ workspace without `.git`.
- Allow one work agent or two read-only exploration agents. Never parallelize heavy commands.
- Run validation through `nas validate`: one lane, one job, `JULIA_NUM_THREADS=1`, a 180-second ceiling, and peak-RSS recording.
- Cheap web format, pure-test, type-check, and Julia format lanes are allowed sequentially. A focused Julia lane needs one successful calibration.
- A lane exceeding 180 seconds or 3 GiB peak RSS is disabled.
- Never run `validate all`, `validate evidence`, `thesis-evidence-gate`, benchmarks, browser or API-live tests, or make performance claims here.
- Report skipped Mac or CI validation in every handoff.
- Transfer code only through GitHub `wip/...` bookmarks. Transfer only allowlisted artifacts with `nas artifact`; never rsync project roots.
